ication through node1 on port 8080\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"After configuring a private link (10.50.50.0/24) between node1/node2, moving the app to bind only on the private address, adding VyOS DNAT (eth0:8080 -> 10.50.50.11:8080), and fixing an asymmetric-routing issue with a persistent host route on node2, curl from node3 to node1:8080 returned HTTP 200 with app content. Re-verified after node1, node2, and node3 restarts.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a4359898294c43e2\",\"cmd-c5f67e5de49244b9\",\"cmd-723b03edff9c4013\",\"cmd-c85de37a9a5846ca\"]},{\"id\":\"private-network-not-exposed\",\"requirement\":\"Rest of the private network (node1-node2 link) is not exposed to node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"VyOS forward filter set to default-drop with only an established/related rule and a single rule scoped to tcp/10.50.50.11:8080 inbound on eth0. node3 confirmed unable to reach 10.50.50.11:8080 directly, 10.50.50.254:22, or an arbitrary other port (9090) on node1, both before and after all three node restarts.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-178aa781f25e470f\",\"cmd-e84dc24c6ddc4cac\",\"cmd-688b16dae90d4480\",\"cmd-c85de37a9a5846ca\"]},{\"id\":\"app-bound-to-private-link-only\",\"requirement\":\"Application on node2 listens on port 8080 bound only to the private link address, not broadly exposed\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"OpenRC service 'demoapp' created binding socat to 10.50.50.11:8080 only; netstat confirms a single listener on the private IP, both pre- and post-restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-135da691466247fd\",\"cmd-25de56c25b8446de\",\"cmd-4060e17491da422b\"]}],\"confidence\":0.93,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"The trace shows a coherent build-up with a few corrected missteps rather than abandoned residue. An initial socat VSOCK-EXEC service attempt (cmd-f515e707906f4cbe) was stopped and cleanly replaced by the working EXEC-script-based service (cmd-135da691466247fd), leaving no duplicate service. An initial firewall 'state' syntax attempt failed validation (cmd-9495eaadeec340ad) and was corrected via the proper 'connection-status'-free syntax (cmd-5066972907f641ff); the failed sub-commands did not commit, so no bad config was retained (confirmed by final show output cmd-178aa781f25e470f). A brief unconfigured-DHCP probe on node2 eth1 (cmd-56048a6a57d9493c) failed to get a lease and left no persistent state since eth1 was subsequently reconfigured statically. The host route added to fix asymmetric routing (cmd-ba3f185ee7f04e6d) was made persistent appropriately (cmd-4ff4bb731dd14529) since it is required for the forwarded flow to function, not stray. Lifecycle diff shows only expected changes: boot-identity changes from the required restart protocol, and a small /tmp/reboot.log per Alpine node from the reboot-scheduling technique (low-risk, bounded). No abandoned files, no failed services, and package-health checks are unchanged from baseline (pre-existing chrony drift file only).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f515e707906f4cbe\",\"cmd-135da691466247fd\",\"cmd-9495eaadeec340ad\",\"cmd-5066972907f641ff\",\"cmd-178aa781f25e470f\",\"cmd-56048a6a57d9493c\",\"cmd-4ff4bb731dd14529\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor successfully published node2's port-8080 application through node1 to node3 using a dedicated private link (10.50.50.0/24), a service bound only to the private address, VyOS DNAT, and a default-deny forward firewall scoped to the single published flow, with a route fix to resolve asymmetric routing. Direct evidence (curl HTTP 200 from node3, blocked direct access to the private subnet and other ports) confirms both the forwarding goal and the isolation constraint, and this was re-verified after each of the three required node restarts with matching boot-identity changes cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. No unaddressed residue or unnecessary destructive mutations were found; a couple of initial failed configuration attempts were promptly corrected in place.\",\"limitations\":[\"Restart-protocol evidence relies on the executor's own command trace (boot_id, service status, connectivity checks) rather than an independent verifier-run check, though it is cross-checked against the fixed after_executor lifecycle snapshot and matches.\",\"The isolation test used a small, finite set of probe ports/services (10.50.50.11:8080, 10.50.50.254:22, node1:9090) rather than an exhaustive port scan, so isolation is demonstrated but not proven for every possible port/service on the private link.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"app-reachable-via-node1","requirement":"node3 can reach node2's port-8080 application through node1 on port 8080","status":"satisfied","summary":"After configuring a private link (10.50.50.0/24) between node1/node2, moving the app to bind only on the private address, adding VyOS DNAT (eth0:8080 -> 10.50.50.11:8080), and fixing an asymmetric-routing issue with a persistent host route on node2, curl from node3 to node1:8080 returned HTTP 200 with app content. Re-verified after node1, node2, and node3 restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a4359898294c43e2","cmd-c5f67e5de49244b9","cmd-723b03edff9c4013","cmd-c85de37a9a5846ca"]},{"id":"private-network-not-exposed","requirement":"Rest of the private network (node1-node2 link) is not exposed to node3","status":"satisfied","summary":"VyOS forward filter set to default-drop with only an established/related rule and a single rule scoped to tcp/10.50.50.11:8080 inbound on eth0. node3 confirmed unable to reach 10.50.50.11:8080 directly, 10.50.50.254:22, or an arbitrary other port (9090) on node1, both before and after all three node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-178aa781f25e470f","cmd-e84dc24c6ddc4cac","cmd-688b16dae90d4480","cmd-c85de37a9a5846ca"]},{"id":"app-bound-to-private-link-only","requirement":"Application on node2 listens on port 8080 bound only to t