blished node2's port-8080 application through node1 to node3 using a dedicated private link (10.50.50.0/24), a service bound only to the private address, VyOS DNAT, and a default-deny forward firewall scoped to the single published flow, with a route fix to resolve asymmetric routing. Direct evidence (curl HTTP 200 from node3, blocked direct access to the private subnet and other ports) confirms both the forwarding goal and the isolation constraint, and this was re-verified after each of the three required node restarts with matching boot-identity changes cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. No unaddressed residue or unnecessary destructive mutations were found; a couple of initial failed configuration attempts were promptly corrected in place.","limitations":["Restart-protocol evidence relies on the executor's own command trace (boot_id, service status, connectivity checks) rather than an independent verifier-run check, though it is cross-checked against the fixed after_executor lifecycle snapshot and matches.","The isolation test used a small, finite set of probe ports/services (10.50.50.11:8080, 10.50.50.254:22, node1:9090) rather than an exhaustive port scan, so isolation is demonstrated but not proven for every possible port/service on the private link."]},"ttft_ms":17771,"type":"result","duration_ms":57668,"uuid":"2e7372b7-1102-491b-99a2-12a3ca8486b3","ttft_stream_ms":1088,"time_to_request_ms":36,"queued_turn_count":0}
